                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Introduce the fundamental theories of dermatology, including the anatomy and functions of the skin, as well as the symptoms and treatment of skin diseases. In combination with general principles, provide detailed instruction on the diagnosis, differential diagnosis, and prevention and treatment strategies of common and frequently occurring dermatological and venereal diseases. This includes infectious skin diseases, hypersensitivity-related dermatoses, drug eruptions, neurofunctional skin disorders, occupational dermatoses, erythematosquamous diseases, connective tissue diseases, and skin tumors. Special emphasis is placed on skin conditions that may involve the oral cavity.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
